.TH CSV2REC "1" "April 2026" "GNU recutils 1.9.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
csv2rec \- csv to rec converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B csv2rec
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]... [\fI\,CSV_FILE\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert csv data into rec data.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-type\fR=\fI\,TYPE\/\fR
type name for the converted records; if this
parameter is omitted then no type is used.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-strict\fR
be strict parsing the csv file.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-omit\-empty\fR
omit empty fields.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
print a help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a CSV file to rec format:

  csv2rec data.csv > data.rec

Convert CSV with a specific record type name:

  csv2rec -t Contacts data.csv > contacts.rec
